{%- comment -%}
  Purelane <head> assets — fonts + core tokens. Rendered ONCE, from
  layout/theme.liquid, immediately after Dawn's base.css.

  Why once, and why here.

  Every Purelane section used to pull core.css itself so it could stand alone.
  That put N copies of the same base rules on the page, and the copy belonging
  to section 2 lands *after* section 1's own stylesheet. Where the two agree on
  specificity — `.purelane .glass-2 { position: relative }` against
  `.purelane-hero .badges { position: absolute }`, both (0,2,0) — the later copy
  won and the hero badge rail dropped out of position.

  The first fix was @layer. That was the wrong tool: unlayered CSS beats layered
  CSS at any specificity, so wrapping our rules in a layer handed every collision
  with Dawn to Dawn. Dawn's plain `h2 { font-weight: 400 }` then outranked
  `.purelane .d2 { font-weight: 800 }`, and the section headings rendered thin.

  Ordering solves both cleanly:
    <head>  Dawn base.css  →  purelane-core.css   (we win vs Dawn, once)
    <body>  purelane-<section>.css                (section wins vs core)

  Fonts are self-hosted rather than pulled from Google. The design specifies
  Outfit for display and Inter for body, neither of which is in Shopify's font
  picker. The prototype loaded both from fonts.googleapis.com, which costs a DNS
  lookup, a TCP connection and a TLS handshake to a third party before a single
  glyph can be requested — all on the critical path for the hero headline, which
  is the LCP element on most viewports. Shopify's `theme check` flags it as
  RemoteAsset for exactly this reason.

  Both families ship as variable fonts, so one latin-subset file covers every
  weight the design uses. Preloaded so the fetch starts with the HTML rather
  than after CSS parses, and font-display: swap so text paints either way.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign outfit = 'purelane-outfit.woff2' | asset_url
  assign inter = 'purelane-inter.woff2' | asset_url
-%}

{{ outfit | preload_tag: as: 'font', type: 'font/woff2', crossorigin: 'anonymous' }}
{{ inter | preload_tag: as: 'font', type: 'font/woff2', crossorigin: 'anonymous' }}

<style>
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Outfit';
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 500 800;
    font-display: swap;
    src: url({{ outfit }}) format('woff2');
    unicode-range: U+0000-00FF, U+0131, U+0152-0153, U+02BB-02BC, U+02C6, U+02DA, U+02DC, U+0304, U+0308, U+0329, U+2000-206F, U+20AC, U+2122, U+2191, U+2193, U+2212, U+2215, U+FEFF, U+FFFD;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Inter';
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 400 700;
    font-display: swap;
    src: url({{ inter }}) format('woff2');
    unicode-range: U+0000-00FF, U+0131, U+0152-0153, U+02BB-02BC, U+02C6, U+02DA, U+02DC, U+0304, U+0308, U+0329, U+2000-206F, U+20AC, U+2122, U+2191, U+2193, U+2212, U+2215, U+FEFF, U+FFFD;
  }
</style>

{{ 'purelane-core.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
